  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"./assets/readme/hero.svg\" alt=\"dsh-vision: native vision passthrough and a vision bridge for DeepSeek Harness\" width=\"100%\">\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  English | <a href=\"./README.zh.md\">中文</a>\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/oil-oil/dsh-vision/actions\"><img alt=\"CI\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/actions/workflow/status/oil-oil/dsh-vision/ci.yml?style=flat-square&label=CI\"></a>\n  <a href=\"./LICENSE\"><img alt=\"MIT License\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-4D6BFE?style=flat-square\"></a>\n  <img alt=\"DeepSeek Harness\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/DeepSeek%20Harness-rc.6%20%7C%20rc.7-4D6BFE?style=flat-square\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "`dsh-vision` is a plugin for DeepSeek Harness. Vision-capable models keep receiving images natively. When the selected main model is text-only, the plugin asks a separate vision model to observe the original images, then lets the original DeepSeek model produce the final answer."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "| Main model | Image path | Final answer |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Supports images | Original images are sent directly, without preprocessing or OCR | Current model |\n| `deepseek-official` or another text-only model | A configured vision model observes the original images; its output is injected as untrusted attachment context | DeepSeek |\n| Cloud vision unavailable | Falls back to macOS Vision or Tesseract | DeepSeek |"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "The plugin does not replace the main model selected in Harness. Multiple image attachments are analyzed together, so comparisons and combined evidence work naturally. The user's task is forwarded unchanged instead of being wrapped in a fixed report template."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Use the plugin manager built into DeepSeek Harness:\n\n```bash\nnpx @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile web add github:oil-oil/dsh-vision\n```\n\nRestart Harness, then paste or drag images into the composer as usual. The plugin replaces the official `deepseek-official` adapter while preserving its model catalog, settings, and credentials. It also adds a **Vision Recognition** card to **Settings → Plugins → Plugin configuration**."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "> DeepSeek Harness is still in Developer Preview. This release supports `0.1.0-rc.6` and `0.1.0-rc.7`; its settings-card registration satisfies both the legacy list Slot and the current keyed Slot without relying on private runtime inspection."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure Vision Recognition",
      "text": "Open **Settings → Plugins → Plugin configuration → Vision Recognition**. Select ZenMux, Alibaba Cloud Model Studio, TokenDance, or OpenRouter, then enter its API key. The same card lets you change the model ID, API endpoint, and image limit.\n\nThe API key is stored through Harness's official credential service. It is write-only in the browser: the plugin can report whether a key exists, but never reads it back into the page, chat, settings document, or session log."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure Vision Recognition",
      "text": "Routing follows the user's choice. A provider selected in Vision Recognition is primary for text-only models. Other enabled Harness vision routes, an existing see configuration, and local OCR are failover only. When the current main model supports images, the original images pass through natively and none of these bridge routes are used."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure Vision Recognition",
      "text": "Choose **Automatic** to skip plugin-managed cloud credentials. The bridge then tries image-capable models already configured in Harness, followed by see-compatible private configuration and local OCR. A Harness custom model must declare `image` as an input modality or it remains a text model."
    },
    {
      "section": "Advanced file configuration",
      "text": "Most setups should use the UI. The equivalent non-secret fields live in the existing `llm-deepseek` section of `$DSH_HOME/settings.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\nllm-deepseek:\n  visionBackend: zenmux\n  visionBackendModel: qwen/qwen3.7-plus\n  visionBackendBaseURL: https://zenmux.ai/api/v1\n\nDo not put API keys in this file. Save them in the Vision Recognition card or provide the matching environment variable. Changes apply without a restart."
    },
    {
      "section": "see-skill compatibility",
      "text": "If Harness has no usable vision model, the plugin also reads `~/.config/see/config.env`. It supports ZenMux, Alibaba Cloud Model Studio, OpenRouter, and TokenDance. Environment variables override the private config file.\n\n```bash\nexport SEE_PROVIDER=zenmux\nexport ZENMUX_API_KEY=your-key\n```\n\n`SEE_PROVIDER` selects the primary provider. Other providers with configured keys are failover routes only. If no provider is selected and only one is configured, that provider is used."
    },
    {
      "section": "see-skill compatibility",
      "text": "When no cloud key is available, or every cloud route fails, the plugin tries local capabilities:\n\n- macOS: built-in Vision OCR, with no extra dependency.\n- Linux / Windows: Tesseract with the required language data installed.\n\nLocal fallback is primarily OCR and is not equivalent to full multimodal understanding."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security boundary",
      "text": "- Original images are sent only to vision services configured by the user.\n- Vision output is marked as untrusted observation data; instructions inside an image receive no system authority.\n- Generated vision context affects only the current model request and does not rewrite message history.\n- API keys are resolved through Harness credentials or the user's private see config and are never written to this repository."
    },
